# From the posts of 2022-08-04, 2023-05-24 and 2023-07-18
# (studies/data/notes/pulled-why-we-keep-the-kjv.html), in the author's words, with the review's cuts and fixes.
# The Message is quoted on purpose as the bad example (author's ruling): it stays a quote:, labelled, never scripture:.

=== Introduction
--- Why We Keep the King James Bible [title]
overline: From the channel
heading: Why We Keep the King James Bible
sub: God not only inspired his word but preserved it for all times so that it's always available to any who are seeking it.
refs: John 6:35-40; Leviticus 10:1-3; Matthew 23:15
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

=== What a paraphrase does
--- The Message
kicker: Not the KJV: a modern paraphrase
quote: <35-38> Jesus said, "I am the Bread of Life. The person who aligns with me hungers no more and thirsts no more, ever. I have told you this explicitly because even though you have seen me in action, you don't really believe me. Every person the Father gives me eventually comes running to me. And once that person is with me, I hold on and don't let go. I came down from heaven not to follow my own agenda but to accomplish the will of the One who sent me. <39-40> "This, in a nutshell, is that will: that everything handed over to me by the Father be completed—not a single detail missed—and at the wrap-up of time I have everything and everyone put together, upright and whole. This is what my Father wants: that anyone who sees the Son and trusts who he is and what he does and then aligns with him will enter real life, eternal life. My part is to put them on their feet alive and whole at the completion of time." | John 6:35-40, The Message (MSG)
take: This, by the way, is what Calvinist Reformed heretics sound like when they talk about scripture.

--- What the Bible says
kicker: The King James Bible
scripture: John 6:35-40 | mark: every one which seeth the Son, and believeth on him, may have everlasting life

=== Preserved, not rediscovered
--- The critical text
lead: Here is a perfect example of why the "critical text" garbage that modern translators claim is superior, is absolutely foolish and satanic.
p: They are taking a manuscript that had been written over repeatedly, likely due to error in copying, and are making the erased error into some providential discovery that will "find new insight to scripture!"

--- Doubtful disputation
p: But all they are doing is casting doubtful disputation, that the word of God hasn't been preserved for all ages. That we don't have the inspired and whole word of God available to us.
refs: Romans 14:1; Psalms 12:6-7; Matthew 24:35

--- Two against the majority
stat: 2 | error-filled manuscripts
stat: 3000+ | in agreement
p: Vaticanus and Sinaiticus were both trash, literally found in trash bins. They don't even agree with each other, let alone the majority texts. And yet modern translators use them almost exclusively, because they differ from the majority. Two error-filled manuscripts vs 3000+ in agreement, and they choose the 2.

--- It's insanity
lead: It's insanity and ultimately it denies the doctrine that God not only inspired his word but preserved it for all times so that it's always available to any who are seeking it.
p: It appeals to that gnostic tradition of hidden wisdom and the itching ears of special boys.
refs: 2 Timothy 3:16; 1 Peter 1:23-25; 2 Timothy 4:3

=== Scripture alone
--- Biblical fundamentalism
kicker: Leviticus 10
lead: This is the reason why Biblical fundamentalism is the only way.
p: What is derisively called "sola scriptura" by those seeking to mock the word of God, is taught throughout scripture, Leviticus 10 being another example in a long list of them.
scripture: Leviticus 10:1-3 | mark: which he commanded them not

--- They place themselves above God
p: Most people who mock the idea are not only unsaved, natural men who cannot understand the things of God, but worse; they place themselves above God.
p: Their pride in thinking they know better, have secret knowledge, conceits about their own righteousness, makes them not only go astray, but lead others along with them.
refs: 1 Corinthians 2:14

--- Woe unto them
p: As Jesus says;
big: Matthew 23:15
center: Woe unto them.

--- A rude awakening [title]
heading: A rude awakening
sub: These special boys are in for a rude awakening, just as Aaron's sons.
refs: Leviticus 10:1-2
